pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The same formula and the same binary, proved SATISFIABLE. `x1 = x2 = 1` is the only model and
% it is one; the `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` next door is therefore visibly false without
% trusting any second tool.
%
% This half is also the guard against a bogus fix: a "fix" that simply refused rows with
% extreme degrees would satisfy the negative test and break `variants/honest-substitution/`.
f 2;
sol x1 x2 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
